1. Scheduler will try to schedule on second node to distribute the load only if there is no taint and required resources are there otherwise it will be scheduled on first node.

2. Container will be restarted not the pod even if we have multi container pod then affected container only be restarted.

3. Env variable will be updated only after restart but configmap changes can be updated dynamically if it is mounted as volume and it won't refresh automatically if subpath is used in volume mount

4. Not sure 

5. Yes infact cluster does load balancing in a round robin way and it supports TCP.

6. losing logs sometimes impact RCA and customer trust in case of failure and it should be collected by some centralized logging system

7. No, there are many factors which indicates that application is not working properly even though liveness is working 

8. Stateless applications can be scaled out using HPA and stateful applications can be scaled up using VPA

9. No, we login to container (default one in case of multi container) and we can also specify which container to login

10. Pod describe, event logs, or can check centralized logging system for previous container logs if captured








