2. Ans: Only container will terminate and kubelet will crate new container.

3. Ans: I don't think it is possible while running the pod.

4. Ans: Absolutely not stable it can be instable due to various reason like Node failure, resource issue

5. Ans: Yes, it is default service type of kubernetes and it creates virtual IP and kube-proxy take care the traffic among all healthy pods

6. Ans: Log can be collected using filebeat, fluentd using any log shipper tool and yes, risk is there of loosing logs if it is not collected properly to central log sytem or not used any persistance volume option

7. Ans: No, it is just checking your application is working or not.

8. Ans: Scalling method like HPA(Horizontal Pod Autoscaller) and VPA(Vertical Pod Autoscaller)

